WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.424 --> 00:00:02.145
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:02.145 --> 00:00:05.089
Today's message is: be restless.

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:06.574
Over to you Nikesh Arora.

00:00:06.574 --> 00:00:07.915
(cock crows)

00:00:07.915 --> 00:00:09.076
(rap music)

00:00:09.076 --> 00:00:11.799
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.799 --> 00:00:14.449
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.449 --> 00:00:18.262
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:20.637
- In my life I've always been restless.

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:22.930
I've never been able to
settle with status quo.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.465
Every time I felt that
life was getting boring,

00:00:24.465 --> 00:00:26.366
life was getting unexciting,

00:00:26.366 --> 00:00:28.935
I decided to pick up and move
and do something different.

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:31.454
And I actually never had a plan.

00:00:31.454 --> 00:00:33.604
So, I go speak at places, people ask me,

00:00:33.604 --> 00:00:35.733
so did you have all this charted out.

00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:37.613
And I've never had a plan charted out.

00:00:37.613 --> 00:00:39.390
I still don't know what's
going to happen tomorrow.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.658
As long as you're happy,

00:00:40.658 --> 00:00:42.214
as long as you feel you're
making a difference,

00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:45.057
as long as you feel that your restlessness

00:00:45.057 --> 00:00:46.611
is getting satisfied.

00:00:46.611 --> 00:00:47.444
Which again, is an oxymoron

00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:49.566
because once your
restlessness gets satisfied,

00:00:49.566 --> 00:00:50.399
you're no longer restless

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:51.549
and you have to be restless again.

00:00:51.549 --> 00:00:53.855
So, I've always tried to be restless,

00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:56.597
always tried to do something different.

00:00:56.597 --> 00:00:57.958
I grew up in this country.

00:00:57.958 --> 00:01:01.045
I ended up being an engineer,

00:01:01.045 --> 00:01:03.496
decided I didn't want
to do that for too long.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.645
Which was a bad choice, now
that I'm in Silicon Valley

00:01:05.645 --> 00:01:07.350
I realize I should have
stuck to those guns.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.171
But anyway, decided to
become a business person

00:01:10.171 --> 00:01:12.448
and decided to go to
business school in the U.S.

00:01:12.448 --> 00:01:14.342
I landed there with two suitcases

00:01:14.342 --> 00:01:15.691
and a pair of white socks,

00:01:15.691 --> 00:01:17.270
which I still remember fondly

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:19.421
but that's part of my romanticizing again.

00:01:19.421 --> 00:01:23.330
So, from there on, I graduated
business school again.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.464
I went to work in the financial industry.

00:01:25.464 --> 00:01:26.776
When I was applying for jobs,

00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:28.523
I was told that you don't
have enough finance,

00:01:28.523 --> 00:01:30.249
so since from then I went

00:01:30.249 --> 00:01:32.815
and got two more degrees in finance.

00:01:32.815 --> 00:01:35.177
So, every time I felt
that I've been challenged,

00:01:35.177 --> 00:01:36.833
I've gone and picked up my bags

00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:38.191
and done something different.

00:01:38.191 --> 00:01:39.278
So, I got bored in Boston,

00:01:39.278 --> 00:01:41.089
I picked up the same two
bags and went to Germany

00:01:41.089 --> 00:01:42.563
and decided to work in Germany

00:01:42.563 --> 00:01:44.371
where I didn't speak a word of German,

00:01:44.371 --> 00:01:46.504
and the average peer
group was 50 years old.

00:01:46.504 --> 00:01:48.670
So, there are many moments in our lives

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.885
when we come to that point and realize

00:01:50.885 --> 00:01:53.366
what would have happened if
I'd have gone the other way.

00:01:53.366 --> 00:01:55.454
Or what if the doors had shut sooner

00:01:55.454 --> 00:01:57.372
before you walk into the train.

00:01:57.372 --> 00:01:59.655
And you can go back and think
about those moments in life,

00:01:59.655 --> 00:02:01.548
but it's not about those
moments, it's about the moments

00:02:01.548 --> 00:02:02.991
when you actually walk through the door.

00:02:02.991 --> 00:02:05.228
- I think entrepreneurs, in
general, are pretty restless.

00:02:05.228 --> 00:02:07.083
We are a restless bunch.

00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:09.241
We are not satisfied with the status quo.

00:02:09.241 --> 00:02:11.870
We want to change the way things are done.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.686
We don't like our boss,
we don't like our job,

00:02:13.686 --> 00:02:15.114
we don't like the industry we're in.

00:02:15.114 --> 00:02:17.428
And instead of just
complaining, what do we do?

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:19.442
We make a change, we do our own thing.

00:02:19.442 --> 00:02:22.611
We want to be the change that
we want to see in the world.

00:02:22.611 --> 00:02:24.316
That's what we as entrpreneurs do,

00:02:24.316 --> 00:02:26.605
and it's why I believe every major problem

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:29.531
in the world would be
solved, not by corporations,

00:02:29.531 --> 00:02:32.038
not by charities, but by entrepreneurs.

00:02:32.038 --> 00:02:35.360
I think we hold the secret
to every positive change

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.130
that is coming in a big way.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.144
And so I think restlessness helps us

00:02:39.144 --> 00:02:41.627
in two major ways, and
one is kind of hidden.

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:43.165
The first is the decision to start.

00:02:43.165 --> 00:02:44.153
Right?

00:02:44.153 --> 00:02:45.663
A lot of people have ideas.

00:02:45.663 --> 00:02:47.503
A lot of people want to start a business,

00:02:47.503 --> 00:02:50.437
not everybody does because
they're not restless enough.

00:02:50.437 --> 00:02:51.941
They don't want it badly enough.

00:02:51.941 --> 00:02:54.138
They're safe, they're secure.

00:02:54.138 --> 00:02:55.430
Sure, they'd like to have more money.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.228
Sure, they'd like to have a bigger impact.

00:02:57.228 --> 00:02:59.824
But they have a nice job,
you're making nice money.

00:02:59.824 --> 00:03:02.111
You have commitments and responsibilities,

00:03:02.111 --> 00:03:03.418
and people to look after.

00:03:03.418 --> 00:03:05.330
You can't afford to go
out and do that thing.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.014
You're not restless enough.

00:03:07.014 --> 00:03:07.847
Right?

00:03:07.847 --> 00:03:09.302
You're too safe in your environment.

00:03:09.302 --> 00:03:10.724
And so you don't ever do anything.

00:03:10.724 --> 00:03:13.073
And that's 90% of America,

00:03:13.073 --> 00:03:15.257
you wake up to a job that you hate.

00:03:15.257 --> 00:03:17.033
And so, the restlessness in entrepreneurs

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:19.240
allows us to get started,

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.043
to pursue our vision, to build a company,

00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:24.113
to solve a problem, to be fulfulled,

00:03:24.113 --> 00:03:25.595
to help customers.

00:03:25.595 --> 00:03:26.883
That's what we do.

00:03:26.883 --> 00:03:28.605
The second part of restlessness, though,

00:03:28.605 --> 00:03:30.308
I think is kind of like a silent killer

00:03:30.308 --> 00:03:31.316
for a lot of entrepreneurs.

00:03:31.316 --> 00:03:33.287
What happens in a lot of companies is

00:03:33.287 --> 00:03:35.081
we get bored of our companies.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.717
That's not something a
lot of people talk about

00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:38.378
but it happens a lot.

00:03:38.378 --> 00:03:39.881
It happens to a lot of entrepreneurs.

00:03:39.881 --> 00:03:42.005
They get bored, they get tired.

00:03:42.005 --> 00:03:45.338
Why did you leave that
job to start your company?

00:03:45.338 --> 00:03:46.806
Because it was boring,

00:03:46.806 --> 00:03:47.683
because you weren't learning,

00:03:47.683 --> 00:03:49.309
because you weren't growing,

00:03:49.309 --> 00:03:50.467
because you weren't having the impact

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:51.857
that you wanted to have.

00:03:51.857 --> 00:03:53.076
And what ends up happening is

00:03:53.076 --> 00:03:54.265
at the start of the company,

00:03:54.265 --> 00:03:55.627
the start of your new business

00:03:55.627 --> 00:03:57.639
everything is what you want to do.

00:03:57.639 --> 00:03:59.050
You start building your vision up.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.386
And then somewhere along the line,

00:04:01.386 --> 00:04:03.937
you have customers and
there's expectations,

00:04:03.937 --> 00:04:06.857
and you found the things that
will make you successful,

00:04:06.857 --> 00:04:08.818
and so you keep doing those things, right.

00:04:08.818 --> 00:04:10.870
You find the path to success,
keep doing that thing.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:11.753
Repeat, rinse and repeat,

00:04:11.753 --> 00:04:13.481
rinse and repeat, rinse and repeat.

00:04:13.481 --> 00:04:14.480
Make more, right?

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.576
Go, go, go.

00:04:15.576 --> 00:04:19.667
The challenge is for
someone who's restless

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.379
what happens when you're
just copying and pasting,

00:04:21.379 --> 00:04:22.540
and copying and pasting,
and copying and pasting,

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.603
and copying and pasting,
and copying and pasting.

00:04:25.603 --> 00:04:26.736
You get bored!

00:04:26.736 --> 00:04:28.533
You don't want to do
the same thing all the,

00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:29.366
that's why you left your job,

00:04:29.366 --> 00:04:30.763
you don't want to do the
same thing over and over,

00:04:30.763 --> 00:04:32.672
over and over and over and over again.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.118
Ad infinitum, right?

00:04:34.118 --> 00:04:35.973
You don't want to do that.

00:04:35.973 --> 00:04:38.982
And not enough entrepreneurs
recognize that.

00:04:38.982 --> 00:04:40.039
And so they end up in this spot

00:04:40.039 --> 00:04:41.147
where they hate their business,

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.721
where they've just
bought themselves a job.

00:04:42.721 --> 00:04:44.073
And they're saying I
want to do this anymore,

00:04:44.073 --> 00:04:45.017
I want to go start something new,

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.125
I want to sell this business,

00:04:46.125 --> 00:04:47.780
I want to move on to something else.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:50.279
Where the real trick
to solving this problem

00:04:50.279 --> 00:04:53.889
is constant and neverending restlessness

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:56.451
and improvement in your business.

00:04:56.451 --> 00:04:59.128
Once you find what made you successful,

00:04:59.128 --> 00:05:02.642
keep doing that, and then try to beat it.

00:05:02.642 --> 00:05:05.751
As you evolve and change
and grow as a human being,

00:05:05.751 --> 00:05:08.603
guess what, you have to
bring that to your business.

00:05:08.603 --> 00:05:10.503
If you are evolving and
changing and growing,

00:05:10.503 --> 00:05:12.271
and your business is staying the same

00:05:12.271 --> 00:05:13.723
and doing always the same thing,

00:05:13.723 --> 00:05:15.126
you are going to get bored.

00:05:15.126 --> 00:05:16.747
There'll be a point where
you've grown so much

00:05:16.747 --> 00:05:18.305
that you don't recognize
your business at all,

00:05:18.305 --> 00:05:20.215
you don't want to be there anymore.

00:05:20.215 --> 00:05:23.693
So, you need to be constantly
introducing restlessness

00:05:23.693 --> 00:05:25.037
into your business.

00:05:25.037 --> 00:05:26.870
As you grow, as you get new ideas,

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.760
as you evolve, you will need to bring that

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.404
to your business immediately

00:05:31.404 --> 00:05:34.178
so that line doesn't get too far apart.

00:05:34.178 --> 00:05:36.399
So that you never get
bored of your business.

00:05:36.399 --> 00:05:39.171
My company has changed a
lot since I first started.

00:05:39.171 --> 00:05:41.537
There's still been that passion
for helping entrepreneurs

00:05:41.537 --> 00:05:43.097
but the execution has changed a lot.

00:05:43.097 --> 00:05:44.569
I never thought I'd be doing YouTube.

00:05:44.569 --> 00:05:46.160
I never wanted to write a book.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.860
I never thought I'd be
working with big brands.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.042
I never thought people
would offer me spots

00:05:50.042 --> 00:05:51.640
on their board of directors.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.233
I never thought I'd be
investing in the company.

00:05:53.233 --> 00:05:55.631
None of this was ever part
of my plan when I started.

00:05:55.631 --> 00:05:57.999
But if all I did was what
I was doing when I started,

00:05:57.999 --> 00:06:01.128
I would hate my company right now.

00:06:01.128 --> 00:06:03.250
You need to evolve your business

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.556
as you evolve yourself.

00:06:05.556 --> 00:06:08.226
Continue to be restless.

00:06:08.226 --> 00:06:10.535
So, the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:06:10.535 --> 00:06:13.833
what are you restless about right now?

00:06:13.833 --> 00:06:15.052
Leave in the comments below,

00:06:15.052 --> 00:06:16.161
super curious to find out.

00:06:16.161 --> 00:06:18.729
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Rick Vasquez.

00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:20.822
Rick, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:06:20.822 --> 00:06:21.919
Your One Word.

00:06:21.919 --> 00:06:23.027
It really, really, really
means a lot to me, man,

00:06:23.027 --> 00:06:24.349
I appreciate the support,

00:06:24.349 --> 00:06:25.818
I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.303
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:27.303 --> 00:06:28.603
I believe in you.

00:06:28.603 --> 00:06:30.484
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:30.484 --> 00:06:32.476
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:32.476 --> 00:06:34.365
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:34.365 --> 00:06:37.277
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:37.277 --> 00:06:38.293
(rap music)

00:06:38.293 --> 00:06:40.165
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:40.165 --> 00:06:43.748
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:06:45.689 --> 00:06:47.546
- Why do you still care enough?

00:06:47.546 --> 00:06:49.199
You're at a point in your life

00:06:49.199 --> 00:06:51.274
where you could go back, you
could do your month in Vegas

00:06:51.274 --> 00:06:52.641
and Florence Henderson could
open up and you could go--

00:06:52.641 --> 00:06:53.640
(audience laughs)

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.897
And hit a couple of balls,
and then some pinball.

00:06:56.897 --> 00:06:59.010
Why do you still care so much?

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:01.264
- Well, I'm not comparing myself

00:07:01.264 --> 00:07:03.291
to any of these people, believe me,

00:07:03.291 --> 00:07:05.063
but you wouldn't say to Picasso,

00:07:05.063 --> 00:07:07.555
when are you going to
put those brushes down,

00:07:07.555 --> 00:07:09.546
get rid of the canvas, you've done it.

00:07:09.546 --> 00:07:10.778
(audience laughs)

00:07:10.778 --> 00:07:11.611
- Right.

00:07:11.611 --> 00:07:13.621
- I'm an entertainer, first and foremost,

00:07:13.621 --> 00:07:14.950
but there's art involved here.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.210
And an artist has an obligation

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.908
to be en route, to be going somewhere.

00:07:17.908 --> 00:07:19.053
There's a journey involved here

00:07:19.053 --> 00:07:19.960
and you don't know where it is,

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.139
and that's the fun.

00:07:21.139 --> 00:07:23.210
So, you're always going
to be seeking and looking

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.446
and going and trying
to challenge yourself.

00:07:25.446 --> 00:07:27.893
So, without sitting around
thinking of that a lot,

00:07:27.893 --> 00:07:30.691
it drives you and it keeps
you trying to be fresh,

00:07:30.691 --> 00:07:32.550
trying to be new, trying
to call on yourself,

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.612
call on yourself a little more, you know.

00:07:34.612 --> 00:07:36.740
- It seems like you're a man of extremes.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:37.933
Like you don't just drum,

00:07:37.933 --> 00:07:40.061
you drum on one of the
largest kits there is.

00:07:40.061 --> 00:07:42.156
You don't just ride motorcycles,

00:07:42.156 --> 00:07:43.832
you ride 50,000 miles--

00:07:43.832 --> 00:07:45.396
- I'm an extremist.

00:07:45.396 --> 00:07:47.592
- Even when you describe your
appetite for reading, too,

00:07:47.592 --> 00:07:49.888
it seems like a voracious
appetite for reading.

00:07:49.888 --> 00:07:54.055
Is that what got you where
you are as a drummer, even?

00:07:55.042 --> 00:07:56.706
- I would expect that it all comes down

00:07:56.706 --> 00:07:58.412
to a kind of restlessness.

00:07:58.412 --> 00:08:00.169
Because when people talk
about boredom, for example,

00:08:00.169 --> 00:08:02.322
I can honestly say I've never been bored

00:08:02.322 --> 00:08:03.750
for a second in my life,

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.532
but I've always found
another way not to be.

00:08:05.532 --> 00:08:07.493
Like if I have to go to a
medical appointment or something,

00:08:07.493 --> 00:08:08.843
I bring a book with me

00:08:08.843 --> 00:08:11.118
so that waiting is not
going to be a hardship.

00:08:11.118 --> 00:08:12.329
In the early days of touring,

00:08:12.329 --> 00:08:13.909
when all that dead time
was hanging on me, reading.

00:08:13.909 --> 00:08:16.871
Portable, useful, you know,
nurturing, all that stuff.

00:08:16.871 --> 00:08:20.454
You learn to adapt to
your own personality.

00:08:21.294 --> 00:08:24.863
The extremes do come in there, too,

00:08:24.863 --> 00:08:28.607
yeah, I wanted to read
every book ever written.

00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:31.116
Drumming wise, my determination

00:08:31.116 --> 00:08:33.590
was more important than talent early on.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.056
I think for most things,
you do have to have

00:08:35.056 --> 00:08:36.340
a bit of a knack,

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.790
but I had to work so hard
to learn so many things,

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:43.299
but I was relentless in
terms of determination.

00:08:43.299 --> 00:08:45.662
And with traveling, when I've got a day,

00:08:45.662 --> 00:08:48.132
I'm tempted by what's the
most excellent thing I can do.

00:08:48.132 --> 00:08:50.495
Which might be way too far, way too long,

00:08:50.495 --> 00:08:52.119
but I'm going to go for that

00:08:52.119 --> 00:08:54.356
because it's the most
excellent thing I can do.

00:08:54.356 --> 00:08:57.031
And with writing, it just seems
unstinting in the same way

00:08:57.031 --> 00:09:01.525
because I just kind of know
when I've done my best on it.

00:09:01.525 --> 00:09:03.813
And maybe an editor can
help make it better,

00:09:03.813 --> 00:09:05.704
and maybe somebody else
could have written it better,

00:09:05.704 --> 00:09:07.320
but I have a good built-in sense

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.621
of this is the best I can do.

00:09:08.621 --> 00:09:10.288
- All I want to do is,

00:09:11.571 --> 00:09:13.225
are good scripts.

00:09:13.225 --> 00:09:17.177
However, they have to manifest themselves.

00:09:17.177 --> 00:09:18.310
- [Interviewer] Have
you ever had an agenda?

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:19.143
- I never have.

00:09:19.143 --> 00:09:20.618
Have you ever been in that mindset?

00:09:20.618 --> 00:09:23.535
- I never have, I never had like a,

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.898
I'm too restless.

00:09:26.898 --> 00:09:29.639
I don't know what I want to do,

00:09:29.639 --> 00:09:31.811
but I know what I don't want to do.

00:09:31.811 --> 00:09:34.523
I can answer the question like that.

00:09:34.523 --> 00:09:38.192
I don't want to do the same type
of movie over and over again.

00:09:38.192 --> 00:09:40.230
I wouldn't want to just be doing comedies.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.657
I wouldn't want to just be doing

00:09:42.657 --> 00:09:45.067
suspense movies or action movies.

00:09:45.067 --> 00:09:47.150
I always want to mix it up.

